<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-v-margrave-of-brandenburg"><span class="enc-name">Otto V, Margrave of Brandenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Otto V, called the Long, was a margrave of Brandenburg of the Ascanian house.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otto-von-bismarck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Otto von Bismarck</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Otto von Bismarck was a Prussian statesman who unified Germany and served as the first chancellor of the German Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-wille-kuusinen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otto-wille-kuusinen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Otto Wille Kuusinen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Otto Wille Kuusinen was a Finnish communist who fled to Soviet Russia after the Finnish Civil War of 1918 and became a leading figure of the Comintern.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-prince-of-stolberg-wernigerode"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otto-prince-of-stolberg-wernigerode.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Otto, Prince of Stolberg-Wernigerode</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Otto, Prince of Stolberg-Wernigerode, was a German statesman and head of his family's Harz lands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-mathilde-cross"><span class="enc-name">Otto-Mathilde Cross</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Otto-Mathilde Cross is a jewelled processional cross made around 982 for Essen Abbey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-